||| Build-time selection of the (Machine, Backend, Hardware) triple that
||| examples target. Generated from this template by the Makefile rule at
||| `Makefile`'s BUILDCONFIG_IDR target, which observes `PRIMARY` +
||| `HARDWARE` + `MACHINE` at build time and substitutes the chosen type
||| tags into this template via sed.
|||
||| The Executor and DType drop out of the chosen triple via the
||| `Preset` typeclass: `Preset PrimaryBackend ChosenHardware` resolves
||| to the `(presetExecutor, presetDType)` cell, and `Provides
||| ChosenMachine ChosenHardware` enforces at compile time that the
||| requested Hardware is actually reachable on the chosen Machine.
|||
||| Mismatched combinations (e.g. PRIMARY=tape HARDWARE=metal, or
||| MACHINE=mac-m-series HARDWARE=cuda) fail at example-compile with
||| clear "no instance Preset …" / "no instance Provides …" errors —
||| not at runtime.
|||
||| Idris-2 cannot drive type-level selection from a runtime env var —
||| types are fixed at elaboration. The generated `BuildConfig.idr` is
||| in `.gitignore`.
|||
||| Do not edit `BuildConfig.idr` directly — your changes will be
||| clobbered on the next build. Edit this `.in` file instead.
module BuildConfig

import public Ml.Executor
import Ml.BackendLib
import Ml.Hardware
import public Ml.Machine
import public Ml.Machine.Verify
import public Ml.Machine.BuiltinChecks
import Ml.Preset

||| The Machine the build targets, sed-substituted from $(MACHINE).
||| Declared at kind `Machine` (the kind alias from the `Machine`
||| module — same as `Type`) so the `MachineRuntimeCheck` instance
||| resolves cleanly under `requireMachine {m = ChosenMachine}`.
public export
ChosenMachine : Machine
ChosenMachine = @CHOSEN_MACHINE_TAG@

||| The primary Backend, sed-substituted from $(PRIMARY).
public export
PrimaryBackend : Type
PrimaryBackend = @PRIMARY_BACKEND_TAG@

||| The Hardware the example default targets, sed-substituted from
||| $(HARDWARE). Must satisfy Provides ChosenMachine ChosenHardware
||| and Preset PrimaryBackend ChosenHardware.
public export
ChosenHardware : Type
ChosenHardware = @CHOSEN_HARDWARE_TAG@

||| Example default Executor — sed-substituted directly from
||| `(PrimaryBackend, ChosenHardware)` per the Preset typeclass's
||| canonical mapping. Equivalent to `presetExecutor {b=PrimaryBackend}
||| {h=ChosenHardware}`, but spelled as a concrete type so downstream
||| typeclass constraints (`UserExecutorTraining ExampleExecutor`)
||| reduce cleanly during elaboration. Idris-2 typeclass methods don't
||| unfold during constraint search; emitting the resolved type avoids
||| the `UserExecutorTraining (presetExecutor ...)` constraint that
||| can't find an instance.
public export
ExampleExecutor : Type
ExampleExecutor = @EXAMPLE_EXECUTOR_TYPE@

||| Example default DType — sed-substituted directly (same reason as
||| ExampleExecutor above).
public export
ExampleDType : Type
ExampleDType = @EXAMPLE_DTYPE_TYPE@

||| Compile-time coherence checks. Resolving these names at module-load
||| forces typeclass resolution to fire — if either instance is missing,
||| the build fails with a clear "no instance" message rather than at
||| an arbitrary example use site.
public export
machineProvidesHardware : Provides ChosenMachine ChosenHardware
machineProvidesHardware = %search

public export
backendHasPreset : Preset PrimaryBackend ChosenHardware
backendHasPreset = %search
